  "description_short": "Step back in time at this vibrant 60s-themed diner serving hearty breakfasts and classic American comfort food.",
  "description_long": "Tucked in the adventure capital of Storms River, Marilyn's 60's Diner is a nostalgic escape with chrome accents, vintage memorabilia, and a jukebox setting the scene. The menu leans into American diner classics done properly – think generous breakfasts with all the trimmings, juicy burgers, milkshakes, and proper chips that keep hikers and families coming back.\n\nThe atmosphere is lively without being loud, making it equally suited to refuelling after a Tsitsikamma trail or settling in with the kids for a relaxed meal. Portions are honest and prices fair, which matters when you're exploring the Garden Route. It's the kind of place that doesn't take itself too seriously but takes its food seriously enough.\n\nLocated on Darnell Street in the heart of Stormsrivier village, it's an easy stop whether you're passing through or based nearby. The retro vibe is genuine rather than gimmicky, and the staff keep things moving even when it's packed with tourists and locals alike.",
